## Local setup

### Prerequisites

- Node.js 18+ or newer
- npm
- A Supabase project

### Install

```bash
git clone https://github.com/evabardhoku/xoxo-tell-her.git
cd xoxo-tell-her
npm install
```

### Environment variables

Create a local `.env` file from the example and fill in your own values.

```bash
cp .env.example .env
```

Example values:

```env
SUPABASE_PROJECT_ID="your-project-id"
SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY="your-publishable-key"
SUPABASE_URL="https://your-project.supabase.co"
VITE_SUPABASE_PROJECT_ID="your-project-id"
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY="your-publishable-key"
VITE_SUPABASE_URL="https://your-project.supabase.co"
```

### Run locally

```bash
npm run dev
```

## Development notes

This project includes a strong emphasis on:

- access control and privacy checks
- trusted social graph behavior
- anonymous content boundaries
- moderation and abuse prevention
- private AI reflection without exposing hidden source context

